<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajaraja Chola III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1216–1256</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajaraja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> III was king of the declining Chola dynasty from 1216 to 1256. Under him the Chola kingdom was overrun by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>, and around 1231 he was captured by the Kadava chief Kopperunchinga, being freed only through the intervention of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> king Narasimha II. The Cholas thereafter depended on Hoysala protection.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaraja-chola-iii.jpg" alt="Rajaraja Chola III" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajaraja3_territories.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
